 {"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-09-06T19:31:08.323Z","evidence":{"commit":"b44d4f24371d8ff1edc4195e14f9431e00c6b192"},"dir_anchors":["lib/apps/fabro-server/src","lib/components/fabro-automation/src"],"name":"automation-breaker-high-water-baseline","description":"Automation circuit breaker (fabro-3d97): per-trigger counters are store-backed with a last-processed-run high-water mark (automation_triggers.breaker_* columns); on first observation or after a replace (the enable path rewrites trigger rows) the newest terminal run becomes the baseline WITHOUT counting, which is what makes 'resume resets the counter' work — a stateless tail-count would instantly re-pause after re-enable. Also: run_summaries.list_all/list_terminal_for_automation return NEWEST-FIRST; scheduler tests must sort by created_at before indexing runs by fire order.","files":["docs/public/api-reference/fabro-api.yaml","lib/apps/fabro-server/src/serve.rs","lib/apps/fabro-server/src/server.rs","lib/apps/fabro-server/src/server/automation_scheduler.rs","lib/apps/fabro-server/src/server/tests.rs","lib/apps/fabro-server/src/test_support.rs","lib/components/fabro-automation/src/error.rs","lib/components/fabro-automation/src/lib.rs","lib/components/fabro-automation/src/model.rs","lib/components/fabro-automation/src/store.rs","lib/components/fabro-automation/tests/store.rs","lib/components/fabro-slack/src/blocks.rs","lib/components/fabro-store/src/run_summary_store.rs","lib/foundation/fabro-api/tests/automation_round_trip.rs","lib/packages/fabro-api-client/src/models/automation-schedule-trigger.ts"],"id":"mx-6cddf3"}
